  year     = {2022},
  note     = {Source: lumbar_spine_mri_ai.xlsx},
  doi      = {10.3389/fendo.2022.890371},
  keywords = {Summary & Abstract PDF},
  comment  = {[Abstract-only record - publisher full text not held.] Multi-task ResNet-50 model grading three conditions jointly from lumbar axial T2 MRI: disc herniation (LDH), central canal stenosis (LCCS) and nerve-root compression (LNRC), using one shared backbone and three fully connected heads. Internal set of 15,254 axial T2 images (Fifth Affiliated Hospital, Sun Yat-sen, 2015-2019) split 70/15/15, plus an independent external test set of 1,273 images from a different hospital; two clinicians annotated with international classification systems and an expert surgeon adjudicated disagreements. Accuracies were 84.17\%/86.99\%/81.21\% internally and 74.16\%/79.65\%/74.16\% externally, with substantial to almost perfect agreement (Gwet kappa 0.67-0.85). Conceptually the closest pre-RSNA analogue: several lumbar findings graded together, with an honest external-validation drop of roughly 7-10 points.},
